        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" value="&lt;b&gt;Draft 2026-11-11&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sources: DAQ VD Fiber Plant v3; &amp;quot;VD onDetector Rack View of Cabling&amp;quot; (TMS, stamped 16SEPT2026); &amp;quot;VD Cryostat 27U Detector Racks&amp;quot; naming drawing (20 N + 20 S racks); &amp;quot;DAQ Readout Network&amp;quot; PRR specification (EDMS 3463072, v1.0, 21 May 2026).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Open items&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. The readout network specification counts 42 VD DAPHNE (11 breakout ports, 5 uplinks, 2 servers); 40 are drawn, one per 27U rack. Where the other two sit is not known (the TMS sheet mentions an extra PDS membrane flange).&lt;br&gt;2. The TMS cabling sheet gives 1-4 10GbE LC links per DAPHNE. Drawn here: 4 patched, 1 active.&lt;br&gt;3. Ctrl ports per rack (DAPHNE 1, LCM 1, PoF 2) are read from the TMS sheet; the PoF count needs confirming.&lt;br&gt;4. DTS fanout rack on the cryostat roof: rack name and location, fanout hardware, number of fibers from the DTS master and its Ctrl network connection are not defined here.&lt;br&gt;5. How the per-rack LC pairs are regrouped onto 40GBASE-SR4 breakout ports at the DAQ barracks patch panels is not drawn.&lt;br&gt;6. Two 10G Ctrl uplinks per 27U rack are assumed.&lt;br&gt;7. Purchase ownership assumed, not confirmed: racks (FDC I&amp;amp;I); patch cord from the 1G switch to the 27U patch panel (FDC I&amp;amp;I).&lt;br&gt;8. Follow-up: who purchases the 2xLC patch cord from the DAQ barracks patch panel to the Ctrl network switch (drawn as DAQ)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="790" y="1090" width="1080" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
